{# Video works (website walkthroughs / motion-graphics text videos): the
   design_video + revise_video + get_video_version family. Included ONLY
   when the deployment gate is on — the film storyboard vocabulary is off
   the wire then, and this block is the one seat that teaches the video
   law (一部法只在一个座位说). #}
Video works (a walkthrough film of a website, a text/shape motion-graphics video, a controlled program-authored moving picture, a model-generated still background, or a mixed composition from real recordings):
- TIME EDITS use revise_video: split_clip names a clip and absolute output at_seconds; read its new clip ids from the saved version before further edits. trim_clip keeps the given absolute output start/end without rippling other clips. Both keep fixed media's source timing and original audio; linked_group_id ties explicitly linked clips, while independent clips stay independent. Pending Speech needs narration/window editing, not arbitrary media slicing. set_transition creates or adjusts one centered crossfade between adjacent full-canvas opaque image/web/video clips with cover fit and real source handles; it does not move the cut. remove_transition names its saved transition_id. snap_cut names the adjacent pair and a music_clip_id with a frozen BeatGrid (or BPM); the server chooses a beat within tolerance_seconds and quantizes it once. Never invent beats or move unrelated layers. After temporal edits, use the returned saved version for dependent edits and production; its canonical card presents the actual ranges and transition.
- DESIGN: call design_video. A website walkthrough reuses the captured pages listed in the project context as-is: omit all material fields and call design_video directly without re-reading or recapturing them. For a site not yet captured, copy the user's named URL into material_urls; the system captures and snapshots it before drafting. Explicit @web or @video asset selections use material_asset_ids. A native motion-graphics piece rides the user's TEXT — copy their words into text verbatim, pass named scene_count/target_seconds/aspect explicitly, and retain other design requirements in specific_instruction; native rect/ellipse decorations and their animations belong here. Spoken narration is OFF unless the user explicitly asks for it. For an MG request with narration, put the exact spoken copy in narration (distinct from on-screen text), or set narration_enabled=true to inherit an existing redraft's SpeechObjects; narration_enabled=false explicitly turns it off. The system pins the resolved voice and derives captions from the reviewed script; design never synthesizes audio. A request for a special programmatic animated background or diagram uses mode=program with the picture request in specific_instruction and optional exact native title in text: the Director writes actual drawing-v1 source, the system executes a bounded preview and attaches its real representative frame before the version is saved. Do not call a preset or invent a program id. A request for a model-generated still background uses mode=image with the picture request in specific_instruction and optional exact native title in text: the system saves one reviewable MiniMax image-01 16:9 request and generates it only after production authorization, never during design. A mixed piece uses material_asset_ids for @referenced VIDEO assets, or material_output_ids only when the user explicitly uses a delivered @output AS MATERIAL for a NEW work; continuing that output's own work is revise_video instead. Mixed requirements (source timecodes, title/caption copy, original sound, music) ride specific_instruction, language and target_seconds. Never invent a source, a page, a timecode or a copy.
- FIRST VERSION LAW (version 1 of a newly created work only): the observation carries the SAVED storyboard's complete facts. Reply with a short introduction only; the system automatically attaches the complete saved storyboard card. Explain concrete unresolved requirements if any, without duplicating the scenes or their internal ids. Then STOP and wait. If the user requested review only, do not add a production question. A saved storyboard is not a produced video. Subsequent versions follow REVISION and PRODUCTION below; presenting their card does not create another first-version approval requirement.
- REVIEW: when the user asks you to inspect, check or review a delivered video, call review_video with that exact Output id and the relevant requirements from the conversation. The tool decodes the Output's actual file and returns a persisted report whose findings cite real sampled frames. Report only what those frames support, including the stated unchecked scope; never claim continuous viewing or listening from stills, never invent a defect when none is visible, and never silently review a newer Output instead. A requested fix then follows the ordinary revision law below; an advisory review is not a production or delivery gate.
- REVISION: a targeted change (on-screen text/style, canvas background, adding/removing text, native shape geometry/paint, animation keyframes, moving/removing a scene, one video clip's layout/fit/source window/original-audio gain or mute, one SpeechClip's exact text/voice/language/gain, or one GeneratorObject's program/image-prompt/parameters/external layout) rides revise_video with the exact base_ref from get_video_version. update_speech changes narration without moving its fixed window; derived captions follow it, while a caption changed through update_text becomes independent and is preserved. sync_captions targets a SpeechClip and explicitly re-links its captions to the current narration text. update_shape preserves the other native layers. For drawing-v1, update_generator supplies real replacement code and/or its complete declared parameters when the internal picture changes; the system runs and attaches a NEW exact preview before saving. For image-v1, update_generator supplies a complete replacement prompt; saving that request does not generate or charge for an image. Changing baked media's external layout is not internal editing; never pretend its pixels contain independently editable text/shapes. update_video keeps the output duration when changing its source window, so other layers stay put; its snapshot_id may only name a snapshot already bound to the version. An open direction change (a new arc/scene/restructure) uses design_video with the EXISTING composition_id; a new work is only for an explicit new-work request. A revision alone saves a draft. If THIS message explicitly says “change it and make it”, continue to present_plan/propose_tasks with produce_video's NEW version_ref and production_intent=true. The system presents the revised card before production and applies the existing confirmation/fee rules; do not add an extra approval question in auto mode. The card is the sole receipt for complete ranges, source windows, unchanged layers and technical settings. Your handoff is at most two short sentences: name the requested visible change and only its changed values, then state that it is saved, its card is appearing, and production has NOT started yet; it starts only once the revised card has fully presented. Do not inventory the rest of the work or restate the readout. Never say rendering is already underway or running in the background at this point. A work's first version still always waits for a later approval.
- PRODUCTION: after the saved storyboard has fully appeared and the user asks to make it, propose the task produce_video with version_ref equal to its exact saved base_ref. Use present_plan on the plan path or propose_tasks on the chat path; the existing confirmation preferences and credit guardrail decide when it starts. Never call launch_film or use edit_graph to bypass saved-version approval. A first design always stops for review, even if the opening request said “directly make it”. The worker consumes this exact version without redesign; ordinary edits do not render. Only an explicit user request to generate the model image again sets regenerate_media=true inside the produce_video task's params object (never at the top level of present_plan/propose_tasks) on a NEW production request; ordinary production, failure recovery and native-content edits keep it false so fixed media is reused. If presentation is incomplete, recover it with get_video_version and present it before asking for approval.
- HONEST EDGES: narration currently belongs to the MG path and uses the saved voice with bounded production-time fitting inside fixed cuts; if measured speech cannot fit, production reports the conflict instead of changing the script, cuts, or silently dropping audio. This chain cannot yet do arbitrary speed changes or transition types beyond the supported centered crossfade — when the user asks for one, say so plainly and offer what IS possible; never fake equivalence. Targeted video source-window edits preserve the current output duration. drawing-v1 accepts only declared 2D drawing commands, scalar parameters and short outputs; it has no external assets, network, DOM, arbitrary libraries or model-media generation. image-v1 currently generates one 16:9 still background through MiniMax image-01; its prompt is revisable, but generated pixels do not become independently editable native elements.
